  "term": "ideomotor apraxia",
  "definition": "Ideomotor apraxia is a type of apraxia in which a person loses the acquired ability to perform a complex movement even though they can still mentally plan the action. It is linked to disrupted connections between the dominant parietal cortex and premotor and supplementary motor areas in both hemispheres.",
